# Research Development Workflow

For non-trivial work, follow:

AUDIT
→ PLAN
→ REVIEW
→ IMPLEMENT
→ TEST
→ SCIENTIFIC VALIDATION
→ BENCHMARK
→ DOCUMENT
→ COMMIT

Do not skip planning for architectural or scientific changes.

Do not implement a large milestone directly from a vague request.

Prefer small coherent changes.

Every significant algorithmic change should include:

- mathematical/scientific motivation
- implementation
- targeted tests
- scientific validation where applicable
- benchmark evidence where applicable
- documentation

When a change affects a scientific claim, explicitly check whether the
claim remains valid.

When a change affects the public API, assess compatibility.

When a change affects performance, measure it.

Do not mark a milestone complete merely because unit tests pass.

A milestone is complete only when implementation, tests, scientific
interpretation, and documentation agree.

Use Plan Mode for multi-file or architectural work.

Use Agent/Build only after an implementation plan has been reviewed.